meta {
  name: Get Domain Config
  type: http
  seq: 17
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/agency/domains/config
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{ownerAccessToken}}
}

tests {
  test("returns 200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });

  test("carries the two fields the add form needs", function () {
    const body = res.getBody();
    expect(body).to.have.property("baseDomain");
    expect(body).to.have.property("reservedLabels");
    expect(body.reservedLabels).to.be.an("array");
  });

  test("baseDomain is a bare hostname, never a URL", function () {
    const base = res.getBody().baseDomain;
    // `null` is a valid answer — it means subdomains are disabled here.
    if (base !== null) {
      expect(base).to.be.a("string");
      expect(base).to.not.match(/^[a-z]+:\/\//);
      expect(base).to.not.include("/");
      expect(base).to.equal(base.toLowerCase());
    }
  });

  test("reserved labels are sorted and include the platform's own", function () {
    const labels = res.getBody().reservedLabels;
    expect(labels).to.include("app");
    expect(labels).to.include("api");
    expect([...labels].sort()).to.deep.equal(labels);
  });
}

docs {
  # GET /agency/domains/config

  What a **subdomain looks like on this deployment** — the fixed suffix an
  agency's own label hangs off, plus the labels nobody may take.

  **Module** — none (`@SkipModule`), like every other route on this controller:
  a domain is not a product module that can be switched off, it is how the
  agency reaches the product at all.
  **Permission** — `agency:domains:read`.
  **Branch** — skipped; a domain belongs to the agency, not one of its offices.
  **Data scope** — none. The response is deployment configuration, identical for
  every tenant, and contains nothing belonging to the calling agency.

  ## Why it exists

  The Domains page shows the suffix beside the field so the owner types only
  `texasholdings` rather than the whole of
  `texasholdings.dev.smithfamily.agency`. Less typing, and the half of the
  address with exactly one correct value cannot be mistyped.

  **The browser cannot derive this.** `BASE_DOMAIN` and `PLATFORM_HOST` are
  deliberately independent settings (see `config/tenant-host.config.ts`) —
  nothing guarantees the admin host is a child of the base zone — so stripping a
  label off the current hostname is a guess that breaks exactly when the two are
  shaped differently, which is the normal case for a nested zone like
  `dev.smithfamily.agency`.

  ## Response `200`
  ```json
  {
    "baseDomain": "dev.smithfamily.agency",
    "reservedLabels": ["admin", "api", "app", "assets", "auth", "..."]
  }
  ```

  | field | type | notes |
  |---|---|---|
  | baseDomain | string \| null | The parent zone, bare (no scheme, no port, no trailing dot). **`null` when `BASE_DOMAIN` is unset**, which disables subdomains entirely — the UI then offers only "a domain you own". |
  | reservedLabels | string[] | Sorted. Labels the platform holds (`app`, `api`, `admin`, `platform`, `inngest`, `dev`, `staging`) plus conventional infrastructure names (`www`, `mail`, `ns1`, `smtp`). |

  `reservedLabels` comes from `RESERVED_SUBDOMAIN_LABELS` in `@sfa/shared` — the
  same set `assertClaimableSubdomain` rejects against, so what the form refuses
  and what the server refuses cannot drift.

  ## Errors
  - `401 Unauthorized` — missing/expired access token.
  - `403 Forbidden` — missing `agency:domains:read`, or a platform account with
    no agency context.

  > Creating the subdomain is still `POST /agency/domains` with the **full**
  > hostname and `kind: "subdomain"` (see **Add Custom Domain** for the body).
  > Splitting the field is a property of the form, not of the API: the server
  > composes nothing and `assertClaimableSubdomain` validates the whole name.
}
